          %title Selected writings
          %p
            Saunders MacLane (1909-2005) was one of the founders of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"} Samuel Eilenberg
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/General+Theory+of+Natural+Equivalences"} General Theory of Natural Equivalences
            introduced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            with the notions of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} dual objects
          %p
            Further with Eilenberg he developed of the strong links with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+theory"} group theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
          %p
            With
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henry+Whitehead"} Henry Whitehead
            he gave the first algebraic description of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-type"} homotopy 2-type
            of a space.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://secure.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/wiki/Saunders_Mac_Lane"} Wikipedia entry
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.genealogy.math.ndsu.nodak.edu/id.php?id=834"} MathGenealogy page
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www-history.mcs.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/MacLane.html"} MacTutor biography
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Colin+McLarty"}> Colin McLarty
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Last Mathematician from Hilbert’s Göttingen: Saunders Mac Lane as Philosopher of Mathematics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cwru.edu/artsci/phil/BJPSMacLane.pdf"} pdf
